\newlabel{fig:attacktypes}{{3}{3}{Walker2d, $\rho =0.3$, random corruption, broken down by which component is corrupted. RDT improves on DT under action and reward corruption, ties under mixed, and \emph {loses} under state-only corruption.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces State-attack anomaly across environments. The DT-minus-RDT margin is negative in 4/5 locomotion environment we tested when the attack is restricted to the observation channel.\relax }}{3}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
